canadians appear to be nearly split when  it comes to protests having an influence  and loosening pandemic restrictions and  ips's poll exclusive to global news  conducted after police enforcement began  in ottawa shows 54 percent of canadians  believe the nationwide trunk or protest  had at least some effect on provincial  government's easing restrictions the  majority of canadians disapprove of how  justin trudeau handled the protest with  57 percent not happy with how the prime  minister dealt with proceedings  conservative party leaders and the  truckers themselves also had a majority  disproving of their handling of the  situation but when it comes to how the  protests in ottawa came to an end the  majority of canadians nearly six in ten  saying they believe they were dealt with  in the best possible way given the  circumstances so when we take a look at  the prime minister's  approval in terms of how people believe  he actually handled this protest only 43  percent actually approve of his  performance which is only seven points  ahead of what the uh the public thinks  about how the truckers performed during  this  uh to during the protest which was 36  percent so  not especially a strong performance here  from the prime minister but what's  particularly worrying is that 52 of the  people that we interviewed said that the  prime minister's divisive rhetoric and  the way that he approached the protest  was  mostly responsible for what happened now  they also looked at other things as  being mostly responsible but it was  really surprising to see that level of  animosity among the public about how the  the prime minister characterized what  was going on with this protest the  surprising part for me is while the  truckers don't do  you know don't score in the majorities  on most things you know 46 percent of  the people that we interviewed said that  while they not may not agree with the  tactics they they actually uh sympathize  with the frustration that's being uh  expressed through this and and what's  interesting about that is that um that's  exactly the same number that we had in  our polling about two weeks ago so as  bad as things got during the course of  the the protest it really didn't affect  how people felt about the protesters  themselves which was surprising  and also when you look at the degree of  of sympathy that exists for example like  on economic issues and and the degree  which people are frustrated by that  about 48 percent of the people that we  interviewed said that this protest  probably wouldn't have taken place if  people weren't feeling the level of  economic frustration that they're  feeling  and finally on this point uh 54 of the  people we interviewed actually agree  that that the uh the fact that we're uh  reducing or loosening some of the  coveted restrictions can be attributed  to uh to the fact that these protests  took place so uh the issue here is that  uh even though uh authorities may not  like it uh what what they're seeing uh  from the response from the public is  actually what the what the the  protesters were doing had a certain  amount of sympathy among the canadian  population close to half of the people  we interviewed and on top of that that  it was effective uh 54 said it at least  had some contributing effect on whether  or not we would be loosening the coveted  restrictions the prime minister's had a  series of choices to make about how he's  wanted to characterize  people through the course of this uh  through the course of this pandemic and  he he chose a particular path during the  election campaign and once he got out of  the election campaign he kept right on  that path and characterized the people  who were part of this protest as being  like the the people that he was  criticizing during the election campaign  now arguably he was talking about people  who are voting uh for uh the opposition  parties particularly the people's party  but also the conservative party he took  exactly that same tack through the  course of this uh uh through the course  of this protest and preferred to see uh  the people who were protesting in those  types of partisan terms and what we're  seeing in in these data is not that um  it's not that people are particularly  united around any sort of partisan  choice this is really  a group of the population you know  roughly 40 percent sometimes a bit more  than that sometimes a bit less than that  who really are feeling left out left  behind and very concerned about the way  that the the government's not only  managing the pandemic but also the way  that uh the economy is going right now  and really they have a very challenged  sense of hope but it's not defined in  partisan terms the prime minister chose  to define it in those terms and the  reaction from the public to that has  been quite negative as we've seen in the  in the polling results 52 of the  population saying he added fuel to the  fire so if people are looking at winning  winners and losers in this there doesn't  seem to be any winners at all uh the  truckers at best uh opinion divided uh  usually losing a 60-40 battle maybe 40  percent of the population being aligned  with them but  not particularly winning the prime  minister's performance not seen as  particularly good in fact everybody  provincial premiers the the opposition  parties the conservative party not doing  particularly well through this at all so  there really are no winners in in  anything that uh that happened during  this protest this is the most divided  and frustrated i can ever remember  seeing canadian public opinion and it  doesn't seem that there's any leadership  on the horizon either in any of the  major opposition parties the  conservatives the ndp but particularly  among in the government where people  would most expect to find leadership  that is making this situation better  so we come out of this uh this series of  protests as a very divided uh unstable  uh country in terms of how the public is  feeling about things right now and one  is looking for signs of hope in the data  and we're just not seeing it
 

